BT 1 0 0 1 0 91.102 Tm 16.5 TL /F1 11 Tf .14902 .145098 .117647 rg (The uploaded manuscript reports neural correlates of stillness in the IBL Brain-Wide Map: 53,136) Tj T* (neurons from 389 sessions and 130 mice, recorded during the passive grey screen after the task,) Tj T* (with ") Tj (moving) Tj (" defined from wheel, lick and face motion in 50 ms bins. Its main findings are lower) Tj T* (firing in stillness \(log2 rate ratio -0.43, 129 of 130 mice\), a stable minority of still-preferring neurons) Tj T* (\(about 15%, against about 40% movement-preferring\), the strongest movement modulation in) Tj T* (brainstem and thalamus, and a rise in firing 0.3 to 0.5 s before movement onset.) Tj T* ET
